#@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"
#@type = "provisioning.integration"

Feature:  Koroneiki to Provisioning External Link Integration
	Testing to assure that koroneiki account external links transfer properly to the account details page.

Setup:
	* I get all test passwords and admin emails
	* I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	* I generate a provisioning company name
	* I generate a provisioning project name
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.koroneiki1                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki1                           |
	* I create a user with the following parameters
	| Screen Name   | pro.koroneiki2                       |
	| Email Address | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| First Name    | PRO                                  |
	| Last Name     | Koroneiki2                           |

Teardown:
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the first default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Onepro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the second default user ID variable
	* I get the ID of the default user belonging to the organization "Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I rename the third default user ID variable
	* I tear down the teams on koroneiki with the following names
	| Koroneiki Partner |
	| Updated Partner   |
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| PROKORKORPRO |
	| PROKOR       |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following names
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I tear down the accounts on koroneiki with the following "Code" values
	| PROKORKORPRO |
	| PROKOR       |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from customer.liferay.com
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from koroneiki
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from provisioning
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the contacts on koroneiki with the following email addresses
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from okta
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I tear down the users with the following screen names from koroneiki
	| pro.koroneiki1       |
	| pro.koroneiki2       |
	| provisionings.worker |
	* I tear down the users with the following screen names from okta
	| pro.koroneiki1       |
	| pro.koroneiki2       |
	| provisionings.worker |
	* I teardown the tickets with the following keywords from zendesk.liferay.com
	| New Subscription(s) for Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| New Subscription(s) for Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I obtain the IDs of the following user email addresses from zendesk.liferay.com
	| pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	| pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken |
	* I teardown users with the following userIds "${staticUserIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com if still present
	| Korpro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Onepro - ${staticProjectName} |
	| Prokor - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId1}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId2}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	* I teardown the user with userId "${staticDefaultUserId3}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: View external link
	@ help.center.acceptance = "true"
	@ help.center.smoke = "true"
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and adding an external link and viewing the external link in the provisioning account details page

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	Then the support organization with the code "PROKORKORPRO" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I create an external link for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | koroneikiautomotive |
	| Entity Id   | 1234                |
	| Entity Name | KoroneikiAutomotive |
	And I get the organization ID of the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I expand the side panel on the account details page
	And I click on the "External Links" side panel tab
	Then I should be able to view the account external link "Salesforce Account"
	And I should be able to view the account external link "Dossiera Project"
	And I should be able to view the account external link "Salesforce Project"
	And I should be able to view the account external link "Zendesk Organization"
	And I should be able to view the account external link "koroneikiautomotive-KoroneikiAutomotive"
	When I click on the "History" tab
	Then the history entry number "1" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "entityId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link  |
	| Update Field Name           | entityId                    |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                         |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticDossieraAccountKey} |
	And the history entry number "1" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "entityName" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | entityName                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | account                    |
	And the history entry number "1" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "domain" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | domain                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | salesforce                 |
	And the history entry number "2" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "entityId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link  |
	| Update Field Name           | entityId                    |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                         |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticDossieraProjectKey} |
	And the history entry number "2" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "entityName" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | entityName                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | project                    |
	And the history entry number "2" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "domain" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | domain                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | dossiera                   |
	And the history entry number "3" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "entityId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link    |
	| Update Field Name           | entityId                      |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                           |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey} |
	And the history entry number "3" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "entityName" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | entityName                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | project                    |
	And the history entry number "3" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "domain" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | domain                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | salesforce                 |
	And the history entry number "4" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "entityId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link|
	| Update Field Name           | entityId                  |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                       |
	| Update Field New Value      | ${staticOrganizationID}   |
	And the history entry number "4" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "entityName" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | entityName                 |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | organization               |
	And the history entry number "4" with the keyword "Auto > Added External Link" with the field value "domain" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Auto > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | domain                     |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                        |
	| Update Field New Value      | zendesk                    |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Added External Link" with the field value "entityId" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | entityId                                            |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | 1234                                                |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Added External Link" with the field value "entityName" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | entityName                                          |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | KoroneikiAutomotive                                 |
	And the history entry with the keyword "Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Added External Link" with the field value "domain" should be visible on the account details page with the following values
	| Update Description          | Koroneiki QA Service Producer > Added External Link |
	| Update Field Name           | domain                                              |
	| Update Field Original Value | N/A                                                 |
	| Update Field New Value      | koroneikiautomotive                                 |

Scenario: View mapped external links
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and adding a mapped external link and viewing the external link in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}              |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                |
	| Address Country                        | United States                              |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                      |
	| Address Region                         | California                                 |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                            |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                        |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                 |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}               |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}               |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                            |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                          |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                           |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                 |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken       |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                        |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                 |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                      |
	| Product Type                           | New                                        |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Digital Enterprise - Prod Sizing 4 |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}              |
	| Renewal                                | false                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}          |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2} |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                 |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                              |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                               |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}            |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}              |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                          |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                        |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                         |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                   |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                        |
	Then the support organization with the code "PROKORKORPRO" should be part of the support site
	And the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I get the organization ID of the organization "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" from zendesk.liferay.com
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "${staticProvisioningAdminEmailAddress}" with password "${staticProvisioningAdminPassword}"
	And I go to the account index page
	And I search the accounts page using the keyword "Korpro"
	And I click on the account with the name "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" on the provisioning index
	And I expand the side panel on the account details page
	And I click on the "External Links" side panel tab
	Then I should be able to view the account external link "Salesforce Account" with the href "https://liferay.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/Account/${staticDossieraAccountKey}/view"
	And I should be able to view the account external link "Salesforce Project" with the href "https://liferay.lightning.force.com/lightning/r/Project__c/${staticSalesforceProjectKey}/view"
	And I should be able to view the account external link "Zendesk Organization" with the href "https://liferaysupport1528999723.zendesk.com/agent/organizations/${staticOrganizationID}/tickets"

Scenario: View external links for Analytics Cloud products
	Testing the ability to create a platinum subcription in Dossiera and adding analytics cloud and lcs external links and viewing the external links in the provisioning account details page 

	Given I publish a project with no partner RabbitMQ message with routing key "dossiera.provisioning.create" with the following values
	| Account Name                           | Prokor - ${staticCompanyName}                   |
	| Address City                           | Diamond Bar                                     |
	| Address Country                        | United States                                   |
	| Address Postal Code                    | 91765                                           |
	| Address Region                         | California                                      |
	| Address Street                         | 456 Fake Street                                 |
	| Contact Email Address                  | pro.koroneiki1@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Contact First Name                     | PRO                                             |
	| Contact Last Name                      | Koroneiki1                                      |
	| Dossiera Account Key                   | ${staticDossieraAccountKey}                     |
	| Dossiera Address Key 1                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey1}                    |
	| Dossiera Address Key 2                 | ${staticDossieraAddressKey2}                    |
	| Dossiera Contact Key                   | ${staticDossieraContactKey}                     |
	| Dossiera Project Key                   | ${staticDossieraProjectKey}                     |
	| End Day                                | ${staticEndDay}                                 |
	| End Month                              | ${staticEndMonth}                               |
	| End Year                               | ${staticEndYear}                                |
	| Industry                               | Automotive                                      |
	| Owner Email Address                    | pro.koroneiki2@lrcustomer.com.broken            |
	| Owner First Name                       | PRO                                             |
	| Owner Last Name                        | Koroneiki2                                      |
	| Partner First Line Support             | false                                           |
	| Product Type                           | New                                             |
	| Product Name                           | Liferay Analytics Cloud Subscription - Business |
	| Project Name                           | Korpro - ${staticProjectName}                   |
	| Renewal                                | false                                           |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Key             | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityKey}               |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 1 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey1}      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Line Item Key 2 | ${staticSalesforceOpportunityLineItemKey2}      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Sold By         | Liferay US                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Stage Name      | Closed Won                                      |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Territory       | United States                                   |
	| Salesforce Opportunity Type            | New Business                                    |
	| Salesforce Owner User Key              | ${staticSalesforceOwnerUserKey}                 |
	| Salesforce Project Key                 | ${staticSalesforceProjectKey}                   |
	| Start Day                              | ${staticStartDay}                               |
	| Start Month                            | ${staticStartMonth}                             |
	| Start Year                             | ${staticStartYear}                              |
	| Subscription Level                     | Platinum                                        |
	| Version Number                         | 7.1                                             |
	And the support organization with the code "PROKORKORPRO" should be part of the support site
	And I create an external link for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | analytics-cloud |
	| Entity Id   | 67890           |
	| Entity Name | group           |
	And I create an external link for the account "Korpro - ${staticProjectName}" with the following values
	| Domain      | dxp-cloud          |
	| Entity Id   | 1z2x3c4v5b6n7m8a9s |
	| Entity Name | project            |
